<article class="post">
<header class="post-header wrap-narrow">
  <span class="eyebrow">Graph · Benchmarks</span>
  <h1><%= post["title"] %></h1>
  <p class="post-meta"><time datetime="<%= post["date"] %>"><%= post["display_date"] %></time> · <%= post["read_minutes"] %> min read</p>
  <p class="post-lede">After the document benchmark we were asked the same question about graphs. So we loaded one graph, a million people and ten million edges, into SoliDB, Neo4j, Memgraph and ArangoDB, and asked each the same six questions. SoliDB 2.10.3 lost most of them, and could not finish a shortest path. This post gives the figures of the build that came out of that, what changed in it, and what the comparison does not show.</p>
  <p class="post-note">Every figure on this page was measured on November 14, 2026 on one machine, each database alone in a container with 4 cores and 16 GB, the harness on other cores. SoliDB is a build of the <code>perf/traversal</code> branch, which is in no release yet. The harness, the settings and the raw results are in the repository, under <code>benchmarks/compare</code> (<code>graph.sh</code>, <code>results/2026-11-14-graph</code>).</p>
</header>
<div class="wrap-narrow"><%- partial("blog/cover", {"post": post, "css_class": "post-cover", "loading": "eager"}) %></div>

<div class="post-body wrap-narrow">
<nav class="post-toc" aria-label="In this post">
