<section id="what"><h2>What was measured</h2>
<p>The graph is generated: 1,000,000 people, each of whom knows up to 18 others, 9,985,098 edges in all. Four edges in five go to people with nearby numbers and one in five to a few people known by many, so that some people are known by very many. Each edge has a year and a weight. People also bought products: 1,499,179 purchases among 10,000 products. Everything is a function of the vertex numbers, so the harness holds its own copy of the graph and computes each answer itself.</p>
<p>Each database is asked six questions, in its own query language and through its own client:</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>The question</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>hop1</code>, <code>hop2</code>, <code>hop3</code></td><td>The distinct people within one, two or three hops of a person, other than that person: how many, and the sum of their numbers.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>filtered</code></td><td>The distinct people two hops away through a second edge dating from a given year or later, who live in a given country.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>fof_bought</code></td><td>The people within two hops who bought a given product.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>shortest</code></td><td>The length of a shortest path between two people who are 2 to 4 hops apart.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>SoliDB receives SDBQL over its native driver, Neo4j and Memgraph receive Cypher over Bolt, ArangoDB receives AQL over HTTP. The queries are in the README, word for word. Every answer is compared with the harness's own, before the timing and during it. A scenario whose first answers are wrong would be skipped and reported; none was, and no timed request returned a wrong answer on any of the four.</p>
<p>The versions are Neo4j Community 2026.10.2, Memgraph 3.14.0 and ArangoDB 3.12.4. PostgreSQL has an adapter too (joins and a recursive query), and it is not in this comparison: it is not a graph database, and the document benchmark already compares SoliDB with it.</p>
</section>

<section id="results"><h2>The results</h2>
<p>Requests per second, median of three runs of 20 seconds, with the median latency in parentheses. One client first:</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>One client</th><th>SoliDB</th><th>Memgraph</th><th>Neo4j</th><th>ArangoDB</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>hop1</code></td><td>61,500 (16&nbsp;µs)</td><td>19,134 (52&nbsp;µs)</td><td>11,289 (83&nbsp;µs)</td><td>10,477 (95&nbsp;µs)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>hop2</code></td><td>28,341 (35&nbsp;µs)</td><td>12,066 (82&nbsp;µs)</td><td>6,837 (144&nbsp;µs)</td><td>2,527 (396&nbsp;µs)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>hop3</code></td><td>2,917 (339&nbsp;µs)</td><td>2,674 (367&nbsp;µs)</td><td>1,621 (621&nbsp;µs)</td><td>313 (3.2&nbsp;ms)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>filtered</code></td><td>14,174 (69&nbsp;µs)</td><td>12,686 (78&nbsp;µs)</td><td>6,940 (141&nbsp;µs)</td><td>1,656 (594&nbsp;µs)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>fof_bought</code></td><td>6,854 (146&nbsp;µs)</td><td>244 (4.0&nbsp;ms)</td><td>2,844 (349&nbsp;µs)</td><td>428 (2.3&nbsp;ms)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>shortest</code></td><td>22,324 (36&nbsp;µs)</td><td>0.6 (1.8&nbsp;s)</td><td>8,309 (104&nbsp;µs)</td><td>7,578 (112&nbsp;µs)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
